<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-4796] Better representation of string-like data in Cassandra interpreter</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-4796</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;With a new driver, columns with string-like data are formatted with single quotes around them, that make data representation look not very good (if they are actual columns, not collections, etc.).  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It would be useful to allow to control. should we output data in CQL syntax, or strip the single quotes around data - that would be useful for plotting, etc. This would match the functionality of the Zeppelin 0.8.x versions&lt;/p&gt;</description>
